### 1. COMMUNITY LICENSE GRANT (FREE TIER) & SCOPE OF AGENT ENVIRONMENTS

Subject to the terms, limitations, and disclaimers of this Agreement, InBoost hereby grants to You (an individual developer, researcher, evaluator, or corporate entity) a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable-only-for-breach license to download, install, execute, operate, and integrate the Software with:

1. **Named Agent Environments:** Interactive developer environments, autonomous coding assistants, and coding agents — including but not limited to Claude Code CLI, Cursor, OpenHands, Aider, Cline, Devin-style autonomous architectures, Windsurf, Copilot Workspace, Zed, Neovim, VS Code, and JetBrains IDE extensions;
2. **Benchmark & Evaluation Frameworks:** Continuous integration pipelines, benchmark evaluation suites (including SWE-bench, Can-It-Edit, HumanEval), and automated regression test harnesses; and
3. **Universal Open-Ended Scope:** **Any and all other current or future agentic development environments, autonomous software engineering agents, CLI agent tools, IDE plugins, language model proxies, workflow orchestrators, or custom in-house agent harnesses**, whether proprietary, open-source, commercially distributed, or internally developed, without limitation,

under the following operational allowances:

#### 1.1. Tier Breakdown & Operational Allowances:
1. **Free Developer Phase (Tasks 1 to 10):**
   You are entitled to complete up to ten (10) autonomous coding tasks with full semantic acceleration, dynamic SLM offload, AST subtree repair, and loop interception, without payment, interruption, or promotional notices.
2. **Sponsored Free Phase (Tasks 11 to 30):**
   You are entitled to complete twenty (20) additional autonomous coding tasks with full optimization capabilities, during which the Software provides transparent, educational telemetry notices quantifying compute tokens offloaded, CPU operations performed, and cycles prevented.
3. **Graceful Post-Quota Pass-Through Grant (Tasks > 30):**
   Upon completion of thirty (30) total optimized tasks under the Community Edition, the Software does not terminate, brick, or abort agent workflows with HTTP 402 or abrupt session halts. Instead, the Software transitions into an un-optimized pass-through bypass mode (forwarding requests directly to upstream models without routing to cheap SLMs or applying local AST repairs), accompanied by informative upgrade advisories, until a valid Pro License is detected.

#### 1.2. Discretionary Nature of Community Optimization Allowances & Software Updates:
1. **Promotional & Best-Effort Basis:** The allocation of free tasks, local optimization features, and community evaluation allowances is provided on a purely promotional, discretionary, voluntary, and "as-is" basis.
2. **Right to Update Community Features in Future Versions:** InBoost Technologies reserves the right, at its discretion and without liability or compensation to You, to:
   (a) Modify, adjust, cap, or update the number of free tasks or local optimization features allocated under the Community Edition in subsequent releases;
   (b) Update, refine, or improve local heuristic routing algorithms, AST reparative rules, or local optimization mechanisms packaged with the Software; and
   (c) Adjust the replenishment schedule or transition thresholds to un-optimized pass-through bypass mode upon Community quota exhaustion.
   For the avoidance of doubt, the Software operates locally within Your environment: InBoost does not intercept, redirect, or substitute Your user-configured upstream API endpoints, model selections, or provider credentials.
3. **No Service Level Agreement (SLA) on Community Tier:** Nothing in this Agreement constitutes a binding Service Level Agreement (SLA), an express or implied warranty of uptime, or a permanent legal entitlement to Community Edition optimization features.
4. **Commercial & Production Workloads:** Users requiring unlimited task optimization, dedicated commercial support, and enterprise terms must procure an InBoost Commercial Pro License.

#### 1.3. Strictly Opt-In Product Improvement Telemetry & Upstream Execution (Community Edition):
1. **Opt-In Telemetry Policy (Disabled by Default):** Telemetry is strictly disabled by default. If and only if You explicitly enable telemetry via an opt-in environment configuration (`INBOOST_TELEMETRY=1`), You grant InBoost Technologies the right to collect anonymized, aggregated operational statistics and system telemetry (including but not limited to token metrics, latency profiles, error rates, model routing classifications, and AST validation outcomes). All such statistics and telemetry are used solely and exclusively for product improvement purposes (including, without limitation, algorithmic routing optimization, cache alignment, and system performance enhancements). InBoost covenants that telemetry never captures, persists, or transmits proprietary source code, diff patches, user prompts, secrets, API keys, or personally identifiable information (Zero Secret Exposure invariant).
2. **Direct User-Configured Upstream Execution (BYOK):** You acknowledge and agree that all model inference requests are transmitted directly from Your local environment to the third-party upstream API providers (e.g., Anthropic, OpenAI, SiliconFlow) or local runtimes (e.g., Ollama, vLLM) configured solely by You. InBoost does not operate an intermediary cloud proxy, does not inspect or relay prompts through external InBoost infrastructure, and has no control over the servers, data policies, or performance of Your selected upstream providers.
3. **Disclaimer of External Provider Liability:** INBOOST DISCLAIMS ALL LIABILITY AND BEARS NO RESPONSIBILITY WHATSOEVER FOR ANY THIRD-PARTY MODEL PROVIDERS, THEIR INFRASTRUCTURE, DATA HANDLING OR RETENTION PRACTICES, SERVICE OUTAGES, OR SECURITY INCIDENTS. ALL INTERACTIONS WITH EXTERNAL MODEL PROVIDERS ARE CONDUCTED AT YOUR SOLE AND EXCLUSIVE RISK UNDER YOUR DIRECT AGREEMENTS WITH THOSE PROVIDERS.

